Mathematics relies heavily on what we call quotients, the traditional ways we group equal things

14:17.300 --> 14:17.760
together.

14:18.320 --> 14:23.660
When classical math creates an equivalence class, it essentially says, take all these

14:23.660 --> 14:30.100
different paths that lead to four, throw them in a bin, slap a label on the bin that says

14:30.100 --> 14:32.060
four, and burn the past.

14:32.200 --> 14:33.700
It just tosses out the history.

14:33.900 --> 14:37.800
It throws away the rich, varied context that led to that equivalence.

14:38.500 --> 14:40.920
SpherePop refuses to throw anything away.

14:41.880 --> 14:47.960
To make two things equal in this system, you must explicitly record a new primitive operation.

14:48.340 --> 14:51.160
Which brings us to the fourth verb, collapse.

14:51.160 --> 14:51.760
Exactly.

